    A15_SMSS_71_M016935_022                                                   
                                                                              
    Apollo 15 Soil Mechanics                                                  
    Lunar Self-Recording Penetrometer (LSRP) Page D1                          
                                                                              
    Post-Flight Load Calibration Plot                                         
                                                                              
    This handwritten plot gives the post-flight calibration numbers to        
    determine the actual load recorded on drum S/N 2002 used on flight unit   
    S/N 2003 of the Lunar Self-Recording Penetrometer (LSRP) carried on the   
    Apollo 15 mission. The plot gives the actual load in Newtons (ordinate)   
    required to produce a given circumferential deflection of the drum in     
    millimeters (abscissa). Six test sets were done on the deadweight jig at  
    the Manned Space Center in Houston. The points are connected by a         
    straight line. Above this line is a second parallel line which is the     
    load corrected for the additional weight of the LSRP (4.86 N).  This is   
    the curve used to reduce the raw data from the LSRP drum and calculate    
    the actual load on the LSRP on the lunar surface.                         
                                                                              
